cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OMEGA PRIME CORE in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "OMEGA PRIME CORE 7.0: open engine for design, calibration and uncertainty quantification of plasmonic LSPR DNA nanosensors"
abstract: >-
  Monolithic, dependency-light (numpy + scipy) engine covering gold permittivity
  (Rakic Lorentz-Drude + additive Kreibig), exact Mie theory for bare and
  core-shell spheres, refined LSPR peak detection with FWHM and bulk sensitivity,
  DNA nearest-neighbor thermodynamics (SantaLucia 1998) with Monte-Carlo
  propagation of DeltaG uncertainty, analytical thermal modelling, and Bayesian
  Langmuir calibration with analytically marginalized S_max, posterior predictive
  checks, identifiability diagnostics and probabilistic LOD. All outputs carry an
  explicit epistemic status. No experimental, biological or clinical validation
  is claimed.
